Search the documentation

Uses full-text search across the Antithesis documentation database. The database is checked for updates before a search, at most once every 5 minutes, unless you pass `offline`.

Prints ranked matches (title and page path); pass a path to `docs_show`. Use `list` to print only the paths.

By default the query is searched as literal text. Pass `match` to treat the query as a raw SQLite FTS5 expression instead, enabling operators like AND/OR/NOT/NEAR, "quoted phrases", `title:` column filters, and `prefix*`.

Examples:
  docs_search {"query": ["fault", "injection"]}
  docs_search {"query": ["config image"]}
  docs_search {"query": ["moment.branch"]}
  docs_search {"query": ["sdk", "setup"]}
  docs_search {"match": true, "query": ["sdk NOT java"]}

With `json`, the matches print as one JSON array of {path, title, snippet} objects, or of paths with `list`.
